            "review_title": "Review at Song Bar",
            "review_text": "alex k\n2 contributions\n0\nWonderful venue, terrible service\nMar 2026 • Friends\nI visited this bar last weekend for sunset drinks after it was recommended by a friend I was meeting that day. It was meant to be a special occasion, as we were having a reunion after not seeing each other for a long time.\n\nUpon arrival, the staff did not ask whether we had a reservation. Instead, the waitress immediately told us there were no tables available and asked us to sit at the bar. However, I had made a reservation for three people specifically requesting a table by the window so we could enjoy the sunset view. I approached the manager and asked if he could check our reservation. Unfortunately, he did not bother to check it and simply said that once a group left, he would let us sit there. Since we didn’t want to spoil the cheerful mood of our reunion, we agreed to wait.\n\nWe then ordered a bottle of drinks and some whiskey. No water was offered. When I asked for water with ice, the waitress told me that they only sell bottled water. Considering this is a bar located in a five-star hotel, I was quite surprised. I mentioned that, to my understanding, refusing to provide drinking water to customers can be considered problematic under Vietnamese regulations. She apologized but made no effort to see if there might be another option. I had expected something like, “Let me check what I can do.” Instead, when I suggested that filtered water with ice would be fine, she abruptly replied, “Please call me when you are ready to order,” and walked away. The tone felt quite rude, and afterward she avoided coming near our table.\n\nWhen we finished our drinks, we spent around 20 minutes trying to find a waiter or waitress to ask for the bill. Eventually, we had to get up and request it ourselves.\n\nOverall, the staff did not appear properly trained or attentive. Perhaps many of their guests are tourists, but that does not justify such poor service.\n\nThe bar itself is beautiful and the view is wonderful, which makes the experience even more disappointing. Unfortunately, because of the service we received, I would not consider returning unless the management addresses these issues and improves their hospitality.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten March 10, 2026\nLinh T\nDear Kalexkkk,\n\nThank you for sharing your feedback regarding your recent visit.\n\nPlease accept our sincere apologies for the experience you described. This is certainly not the standard of service we aim to provide. We regret that you felt uncomfortable and that your concerns were not handled to your satisfaction.\n\nYour comments have been shared with the management team and are being reviewed to ensure appropriate follow-up and corrective actions are taken.\n\nWe appreciate you bringing this matter to our attention and hope to have the opportunity to welcome you back and provide you with a more positive experience in the future.\n\nKind Regards,\nTinh Tran\nHead of Event Operations\nRead more\nWritten April 13, 2026\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
